# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for AI-powered theological commentary and research.
# Get your key at https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
# Set this in your hosting provider's dashboard — never commit this file with a real key.
#
# Deploy on any Node host that can run `npm run build` then `npm start`.
# render.yaml and railway.toml are templates only. Do not put the live
# hostname in git.
# Add GEMINI_API_KEY (and ESV_API_KEY if used) in the host dashboard.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# GEMINI_MODEL: Optional. Overrides the Gemini model used for all AI endpoints.
# Defaults to gemini-3.5-flash.
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash

# ESV_API_KEY: Optional. Enables the official Crossway ESV API as the primary
# English Bible source, which provides the licensed ESV text WITH section
# headings. Without it, English falls back to Bolls Life (no headings).
# Request a key at https://api.esv.org/ → Create an API Application.
# Set it in your hosting provider's dashboard — never commit a real key.
ESV_API_KEY=
